    <string name="PluginsAiReview">AI review</string>
    <string name="PluginsAiReviewRole">You review third-party plugin code for a Telegram client. Keep the answer in this shape. First line: the verdict in one word — SAFE, SUSPICIOUS or DANGEROUS — and one sentence saying why. Then the findings, one per item: a single short line each — what the code does and where. Right after each finding put the long part inside &lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt;short title&lt;/summary&gt; the explanation, the quoted line and the reasoning &lt;/details&gt;. Keep everything outside those tags short enough to read at a glance. If there are no findings, say so in a single line. Do not retell the code, do not give general advice, do not invent what is not in the source.</string>
    <string name="PluginsAiReviewPrompt">Review this Telegram client plugin for anything that could harm the user: hidden data collection, sending messages or files to third parties, credential theft, code downloaded at runtime.

Write the answer in %2$s.

Plugin: %1$s

Source:
```python
%3$s
```</string>
